# Implementation Plan: Local GPU-Accelerated Option Skew Map

This plan outlines the steps to build a local, GPU-accelerated option skew map that ingests option chain data, computes the 25-delta implied volatility skew using a PyTorch pricing engine, and maps stocks into a 4-quadrant sentiment board on a new Streamlit page.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **1. CUDA Acceleration vs. CPU Fallback**
> Your current Python environment has the CPU-only version of PyTorch installed (`2.10.0+cpu`). We will design the mathematical engine using device-agnostic PyTorch code: it will auto-detect and utilize the GPU if `torch.cuda.is_available()` becomes true (e.g. if you install a CUDA-enabled PyTorch build later), and otherwise run via vectorized CPU tensors, which is still highly efficient.
>
> **2. NSE Option Chain Data Sourcing**
> Automated scraping of the NSE website via nsepython/aiohttp is notoriously fragile due to Akamai blocking and dynamic cookie rotation. We propose fetching options data for Indian markets using your existing **Upstox API client**, which is stable, rate-limit friendly, and fully authenticated in the application. We will use `yfinance` to fetch the US options data.
>
> **3. Expiry Range Selection**
> As per the reference document, we will target option expirations **30 to 45 days out** (filtering out weekly and short-term 0DTE options to remove noisy short-term gamma fluctuations).

