### Component 3: Dashboard UI Setup

#### [NEW] [pages/1_Option_Skew_Map.py](file:///d:/Projects/early%20screener/pages/1_Option_Skew_Map.py)
Creating this file in a new `pages/` directory instructs Streamlit to automatically enable multi-page navigation. This page will display:
* **Four-Quadrant Scatter Plot**: An interactive Plotly chart with 1-Month Return on the X-axis and 25-Delta Skew on the Y-axis.
  * **Top-Right**: Hedged Rally (stock up, puts bid) - *Action: Tighten Stops*.
  * **Bottom-Right**: Chase (stock up, calls bid) - *Action: Crowded Trade / Gamma Squeeze*.
  * **Top-Left**: Fear (stock down, puts bid) - *Action: Leave it alone*.
  * **Bottom-Left**: Contrarian Bid (stock down, calls bid) - *Action: Watchlist for Reversal*.
* **Dynamic Sentence Explainer**: Hovering or selecting a stock prints the formatted sentence:
  > **[Ticker]** — traders are paying **[slightly/clearly/heavily]** more for **[puts/calls]**, which is more **[fear/upside]** than **[X%]** of its sector. The stock is **[up/down X%]** on the month, on **[heavy/normal/light]** volume. That puts it in **[Quadrant]**.
* **Filterable & Sliceable Database**: A detailed, searchable table of the skew records with sidebar filters for:
  * Market Segment (US vs. Indian NSE)
  * Sector / Theme
  * Market Capitalization (Size)
* **Compliance Guard**: Strictly filters and ensures that any alerts generated for US tickers specify the purchase of the **cash underlying equity only** to remain compliant with RBI LRS derivative trading bans.

